---
/**
 * @file publicar-restaurante/index.astro
 * @description Permanent redirect to `/planes/gastronomia/`, the gastronomy
 * sales page (HOS-941 D-8).
 *
 * ## Why now and not with HOS-985
 *
 * H6 built `/planes/gastronomia/` and deliberately left this URL serving, for
 * one concrete reason it wrote down: this page still carried the vertical's
 * PRICE inline, and the price only moves down to `/planes/gastronomia/precios/`
 * when H7 builds that page. Retiring the URL first would have left the whole
 * vertical with no price anywhere on the site. Both halves land together here.
 *
 * ## Why `/planes/gastronomia/` and not `.../precios/`
 *
 * This URL's content was a SALES page that happened to also carry a price
 * block: hero, benefits, how-it-works, FAQ, and the card at the end. Its
 * successor by content is the sales page, and a visitor arriving from an old
 * link expects the argument they came for, not a grid. The price block's own
 * successor is one level further down, and the sales page's CTA is what takes
 * them there.
 *
 * ## Why `gastronomia` and not `restaurantes`
 *
 * D-9. HOS-986 is open precisely because "Publicá tu restaurante" reads as
 * excluding food trucks, rotiserías and parrillas — all of which this vertical
 * sells to. The old slug baked that exclusion into the URL, which is the most
 * expensive thing to change later; retiring it is the cheapest this will ever
 * be, since the page shipped on 2026-08-21 (PR #2920) and has accumulated
 * almost no ranking to move.
 *
 * @route     /{lang}/publicar-restaurante/
 * @rendering SSR (prerender=false) — emits a 301 and no body.
 */

import { buildUrl } from '@/lib/urls';

export const prerender = false;

const locale = Astro.locals.locale;

return Astro.redirect(buildUrl({ locale, path: 'planes/gastronomia' }), 301);
---
